WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.170
The Nile's natural flow at Aswan averaged
86.5 billion cubic metres a year,

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.470
1900 to 2018.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:13.790
One paper says about 85 per cent of
Nile waters originate in Ethiopia.

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:21.600
Yet in 1959, Egypt and Sudan shared it:
55.5 billion cubic metres a year to Egypt,

5
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.770
18.5 to Sudan.

6
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.270
Ethiopia was not a party.

7
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.670
In 2011, Ethiopia began
building a dam on the Blue Nile.

8
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.230
Who decides how the Nile is used now?

9
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.010
Egypt?

10
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:34.930
Ethiopia?

11
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.130
The UN?

12
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.170
In this mission, you'll weigh
each country's interests,

13
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.730
from electricity to what
Egypt calls survival.

14
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.270
Then you'll test what the
evidence says a deal would need.

15
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.230
Your mission: decide
who shapes the Nile now,

16
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.490
and what would make a deal work.
